    },
    {
      "id": "I5C4qBwcdpXjw4UN0WWQK",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -12100,
      "y": 8420,
      "width": 877.8004150390625,
      "height": 1120,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bEF",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 774887357,
      "version": 1536,
      "versionNonce": 502243836,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786303613541,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "ToDo: We'll need to work out how to mark an invite \nas \"Claimed\" so somebody can't re-join a game with\nan invite that they've already used.  This could \njust be a standalone \"Invite\" endpoint.\n\nId: string\nSent: timestamp\nGameId: string\nUserId: nullable string (set if existing user)\nEmail: always set, but only really here for logging\nStatus: Pending | Sent | Claimed\n\nthen they get sent to a URL like this after login\nPOST /Invite/Claim { InvitationId }\n\nWould also let us move invites out of the Games section\nPOST /Invite { GameId, [ { UserId, EmailAddress } ] }\n\nWe could use the invitation Id to resolve the game and\nsuch so that we're not exposing loads of ids in encoded\nstrings\n\nIt would also let us represent invitations in the app \ntoo.  A bit of a \"next iteration\" thought once we've\ngot all of the IdP stuff wired up.  Might be a good\nway to do it without sending anything in the meantime\ntoo.\n\nWe could use a cron or event driven thing to set userId \nfor invitations that are associated with email addresses\non create.  Wouldn't really work if the invite went to \none address and they signed up with another, but whatever",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "ToDo: We'll need to work out how to mark an invite \nas \"Claimed\" so somebody can't re-join a game with\nan invite that they've already used.  This could \njust be a standalone \"Invite\" endpoint.\n\nId: string\nSent: timestamp\nGameId: string\nUserId: nullable string (set if existing user)\nEmail: always set, but only really here for logging\nStatus: Pending | Sent | Claimed\n\nthen they get sent to a URL like this after login\nPOST /Invite/Claim { InvitationId }\n\nWould also let us move invites out of the Games section\nPOST /Invite { GameId, [ { UserId, EmailAddress } ] }\n\nWe could use the invitation Id to resolve the game and\nsuch so that we're not exposing loads of ids in encoded\nstrings\n\nIt would also let us represent invitations in the app \ntoo.  A bit of a \"next iteration\" thought once we've\ngot all of the IdP stuff wired up.  Might be a good\nway to do it without sending anything in the meantime\ntoo.\n\nWe could use a cron or event driven thing to set userId \nfor invitations that are associated with email addresses\non create.  Wouldn't really work if the invite went to \none address and they signed up with another, but whatever",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
